-- The last two things proofread wanted after 0049: samagri, and the
-- "why we do it" text every published pooja carries.
--
-- THE SAMAGRI IS THE BOOK'S OWN LIST, book pages 7 and 8, items 1 to 10. The
-- book splits its list at item 11 and says so -- "additional items required for
-- Samidaadhanam and other homams" -- so the kundam, the samidha sticks and the
-- fire-making materials belong to the Samidadhanam placeholder, not here.
--
-- Two items are optional and both are learning aids: a recording, because the
-- svaras cannot be learnt from a page, and a printed text. Marked not-required
-- so the checklist does not tell a beginner they cannot start without a CD.
-- Item 10 is, fairly read, this app -- which makes it item 10 rather than a
-- replacement for items 1 to 9.
--
-- NO NAIVEDYAM, and that is not an omission. Sandhyavandanam offers water and
-- nothing else; there is no naivedyam anywhere in its forty-five steps.
-- proofread used to demand naivedyam of every pooja, which was true of the
-- three it had; it now asks only of a rite that has a step offering it.
-- =============================================================================

